# STM8L151 SDCC linker script (sdldstm8)
# Minimal map to get a firmware linked.
#
# Adjust FLASH/RAM sizes to your exact STM8L151 variant.

# --- Memory placement (base addresses) ---
# STM8 flash starts at 0x8000
# STM8 RAM is typically in 0x0000.. range (direct page) and goes upward
# We'll keep it simple:
-b VECTORS = 0x8000
-b HOME    = 0x8080
-b CODE    = 0x8080
-b CONST   = 0x8080

# RAM start at 0x0000
-b DATA    = 0x0000
-b SSEG    = 0x0000

# --- Sizes (IMPORTANT) ---
# Example for a "medium" variant:
#   FLASH: 0x8000..0xFFFF  => 32 KB
#   RAM:   0x0000..0x07FF  => 2 KB
#
# If your chip has 16KB flash -> use -c CODE = 0x4000
# If your chip has 64KB flash -> still ends at 0xFFFF but more mapped, usually ok.
#
# Let's assume 32KB flash + 2KB RAM as safe default:
-c CODE = 0x7F80
-c DATA = 0x0800

# --- Stack ---
# Put stack at top of RAM (end - 1). If RAM=0x0800 => top=0x07FF
# SDCC linker uses -k for stack? Often for stm8 you set it via startup (LDW SP,#...).
# We'll set it in startup, so no linker stack directive here.

# --- Libraries ---
# SDCC needs its runtime libs. Usually sdcc driver adds them, but sdld sometimes needs explicit:
# If you get "undefined symbol" from libc, enable these lines.
# -l stm8
# -l c
